cting, interacting\". Search methods: initial literature search and expansion methods. Need exact. Maybe \"keyword search\" and \"snowballing\" or \"forward and backward snowballing\". The table topic categories maybe \"Reasoning\", \"Acting\", \"Interacting\". They ask \"作者最初如何检索论文，随后用什么方法扩展文献？\" `search_methods` 英文数组 lower underscore. Maybe `keyword_search`, `backward_snowballing`, `forward_snowballing`. Need exact source.\n\nReasoning: Self Consistency selection rule \"majority voting\" evidenced page10. ToT two search controllers: likely \"BFS (breadth-first search) and DFS (depth-first search)\"? Tree of Thoughts paper uses \"breadth-first search (BFS) and depth-first search (DFS)\" as search algorithms, with states evaluated by LLM. The question says \"介绍哪两种搜索控制器\" - maybe \"BFS\" and \"DFS\" exactly. Need lower, hyphen underscore: `breadth_first_search`, `depth_first_search` maybe. Search page likely 11-13. \n\nTool use: Toolformer five tools: calculator, question answering, machine translation, Wikipedia search, calendar. Exact. ToolBench API count 16,464 from page10 table. Need quote supports all tools, maybe page 15 list. Toolformer tools array shorthand `calculator`, `question_answering`, `machine_translation`, `wikipedia_search`, `calendar` possibly. Need quote exact.\n\nMulti-agent: CAMEL prompting method to maintain roles and cooperate: \"role-playing\" perhaps \"inception prompting\". CAMEL paper uses \"role-playing\" with \"task-oriented role-play\" and \"inception prompting\" to guide agents. Question wording: \"CAMEL 用什么提示方法让角色保持身份并合作？\" likely \"inception prompting\". `camel_prompting`: lowercase underscore -> `inception_prompting`. Need paper says \"CAMEL uses inception prompting to guide chat agents toward task completion while maintaining role identities.\" likely page 36-38. Generative Agents credibility evaluation how many human evaluators? 100? The paper's generative agents evaluation used 100 human evaluators? Let's recall. \"Generative Agents: Interactive Simulacra of Human Behavior\" evaluated believability with 100 participants? It may say \"100 human evaluators\" ranking interview responses. Question asks 可信度评估有多少名人类评估者? likely 100. Need exact page.\n\nOutlook: Table 4 five research topics. Need list exact Topic names. Could be \"benchmarking\", \"reasoning\", \"tool use\", \"multi-agent\", \"safety\"? Need inspect pages 51-52 or 49-50. Conclusion three capabilities benefit from two foundational abilities: \"memory and planning\"? They say reasoning, acting, interacting all benefit from \"memory and planning\" maybe. shared_foundations likely `memory`, `planning`. Need exact.\n\nWe need notes for all five, and then final report. Because remaining calls 5, likely we can:\nCall 1: get evidence key pages in batches but limited by chars. Use get_evidence for overview (perhaps page 3/4), reasoning (10,13), tool_use (10,15), multi_agent (37,42), outlook (51,52). That's 10 pages, maybe 40k chars too big. We can select 6 pages. Tool result can exceed request? Max 32k; need keep under. Each page ~4-8k. Could do 5 pages ~25k. Then next call save notes and maybe more evidence. But final notes must all enter subsequent request. save_note tool result just confirmation; actual notes maybe included in next request automatically? It says final notes must together enter subsequent real model request. If save five notes in one call, next request likely presents latest_notes; then we can write report. That uses one call. Then verify. We have 5 calls: current get evidence, notes, write/verify, maybe fix, finish. Need be very efficient.\n\nCould use get_evidence for pages:\noverview: likely page 3 or 4 states categories and search methodology.\nreasoning: page 10 (self consistency) and maybe 12 or 13 (ToT).\ntool_use: page 15 (toolformer) and page10 (16,464).\nmulti_agent: page 35-37 (CAMEL), page 42 (generative agents).\noutlook: page 51 (table4, conclusion).\nThat's 9 pages. Too much. We can maybe get 5 pages that c